Restart or Force Configuration Reload on Production APIcast Pods
By default, 3scale APIcast gateways poll 3scale for configuration updates periodically (usually every 500 seconds / ~8 minutes via APICAST_CONFIGURATION_LOADER).

To force the Production gateway pods to immediately download and apply the new Routing Policy without waiting:

Run this command on your workstation terminal:

Bash
# Target the project where APIcast is deployed (usually 3scale or 3scale-gateway)
oc rollout restart deployment/apicast-production -n 3scale


ORDER OF POLICY MATTERS


Phase 1: Diagnosing Pod and S2I Build Failures1. Pip Install Failures (Could not find a version...)Symptom: OpenShift S2I build fails with distribution errors when attempting to install dependencies.Root Cause: Build pods lack external internet access to reach PyPI, proxy variables are unconfigured, or the base Python image is deprecated.Resolution:Verify the Python runtime version in the builder image (ensure Python 3.9+).If running behind a corporate firewall, inject proxy variables into the BuildConfig:Bashoc set env bc/bookstore-v1 HTTP_PROXY="http://proxy.example.com:8080" HTTPS_PROXY="http://proxy.example.com:8080"
Alternatively, deploy using a zero-dependency fallback leveraging Python's standard library http.server.2. Pod Fails to Start or Enters CrashLoopBackOffResolution:Bashoc get pods -n api-version
oc logs deployment/bookstore-v1 -n api-version
If a stale pod fails, delete it to allow the ReplicaSet to spawn a clean replacement:Bashoc delete pod <pod-name> -n api-version
Phase 2: Resolving HTTP 404 (Not Found) Errors1. Identifying the Source of 404Symptom: {"detail": "Not Found"} vs generic HTML 404.{"detail": "Not Found"}: Generated by FastAPI directly. The request reached the backend pod, but the path requested does not match registered route decorators (@app.get(...)).   HTML 404 / APIcast 404: Generated by the OpenShift HAProxy router or APIcast. The request was rejected before reaching the backend pod.2. Pod Logs Show GET /?user_key=... 404 Not FoundRoot Cause: In the 3scale Routing Policy, the replace_path field was configured or static base URLs stripped the original /books URI path.   Resolution:In the 3scale Admin Portal, edit the Routing Policy under Product → Integration → Policies.   Ensure replace_path is left completely blank to retain the original incoming request path.   Alternatively, update app.py in both services to decorate both the root and the subpath:Python@app.get("/")
@app.get("/books")
def get_books(): ...
3. APIcast Rejects Unmapped RequestsRoot Cause: A request path lacks a corresponding Product Mapping Rule.   Resolution:Ensure explicit Mapping Rules exist under Integration → Mapping Rules for each valid path format:Verb: GET, Pattern: /v1/books   Verb: GET, Pattern: /v2/books   Verb: GET, Pattern: /books (required for generic header-routed calls)Phase 3: Resolving Header-Based Version Routing Issues1. Both Headers Route to the Same Backend (v2)Check A: Policy Chain OrderThe Routing Policy must reside above the standard APIcast Policy in the chain. If APIcast runs first, default Product backend routing executes before header evaluation.Check B: Header Field Naming in Policy UIInside Rules → Condition → Operations:Set match* to header.   Set header_name* to X-API-Version (do not prefix with http_ or use internal NGINX variable names like http_x_api_version).   Set op* to == (use == for plain text matching instead of unanchored regex matchers).   Check C: Casing Discrepancies in Test ScriptsLua string matching in APIcast policies is case-sensitive. Ensure the test client passes the exact case configured in the policy:Bashcurl -k -s -H "X-API-Version: 1" "${GATEWAY_URL}/books?user_key=${USER_KEY}"
curl -k -s -H "X-API-Version: 2" "${GATEWAY_URL}/books?user_key=${USER_KEY}"
Phase 4: Resolving Staging vs. Production Sync Delays1. Changes Work in Staging but Fail in ProductionRoot Cause: Policies were promoted to Staging, but the Production gateway was not updated or cached old configurations.   Resolution:Navigate to Product → Integration → Configuration.Confirm that the configuration version numbers for both Staging APIcast and Production APIcast are identical.If mismatched, click Promote v. X to Production APIcast.2. Immediate Configuration Refresh on Gateway PodsBy default, APIcast caches configuration states. Force an immediate configuration reload without waiting for polling intervals:Bashoc rollout restart deployment/apicast-production -n 3scale
oc rollout restart deployment/apicast-staging -n 3scale
